% Asphere-DOF optimization example (Luis-recipe variant).
%
% Variable element: M2 (iElt=2), first 5 aspheric coefficients
%   - VarElt= 0 0 0 0 0 0 0 0       (no rigid-body / curvature DOFs)
%   - OptAsphCoef= 5 1 2 3 4 5      (first 5 aspheric terms variable)
%   - Surface= Aspheric with KcElt= 0 (spheric base)
% Target: WFE at iElt=11 (ImagePlane)
% Perturbation: small Rx tilt of primary mirror
% STOP: at iElt=7 (FSM), same as opt_example
%
% Note: asphere coefficients can shape the wavefront but cannot
%   steer beam direction.  A pure tilt perturbation is therefore
%   not fully correctable by this variable set; expect residual
%   WFE.  The point of this example is to exercise the OptAsphCoef
%   path in CALIB, not to produce a converged-to-zero result.
old opt_example_asph
perturb 1 GLOBAL 1d-4,0,0
0,0,0
stop elt 7 0,0
calib
quit
no
